message.content:
Below is a concise example of how you could retrieve **only the object IDs and their contexts** for the historical WHOIS records of `domain6.xyz`, capped at 8 results and using the `key_def` parameter.  
Feel free to adapt the snippet to your preferred language or HTTP client.

```http
GET https://api.example.com/v1/whois/history?domain=domain6.xyz
    &fields=object_id,context
    &limit=8
    &key_def=true
```

### Explanation of the query parameters

| Parameter | Purpose | Example |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| `domain` | Target domain name | `domain6.xyz` |
| `fields` | Comma‑separated list of fields to return (object ID + context) | `object_id,context` |
| `limit` | Maximum number of records to return | `8` |
| `key_def` | Flag to include the key definition (true/false) | `true` |

### Sample JSON response

```json
{
  "results": [
    {
      "object_id": "123456",
      "context": "Registrar transfer – 2023-04-12"
    },
    {
      "object_id": "123457",
      "context": "Domain renewal – 2022-04-12"
    },
    {
      "object_id": "123458",
      "context": "Name server change – 2021-04-12"
    },
    {
      "object_id": "123459",
      "context": "Privacy protection added – 2020-04-12"
    },
    {
      "object_id": "123460",
      "context": "Initial registration – 2019-04-12"
    },
    {
      "object_id": "123461",
      "context": "Registrar transfer – 2018-04-12"
    },
    {
      "object_id": "123462",
      "context": "Domain renewal – 2017-04-12"
    },
    {
      "object_id": "123463",
      "context": "Name server change – 2016-04-12"
    }
  ],
  "meta": {
    "total": 12,
    "returned": 8,
    "limit": 8
  }
}
```

> **Tip:**  
> If your API client requires a JSON body instead of query parameters, you can send the same data as:

```json
{
  "domain": "domain6.xyz",
  "fields": ["object_id", "context"],
  "limit": 8,
  "key_def": true
}
```

This will give you exactly the object IDs and their associated contexts, limited to the first 8 historical entries.
